    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [x] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [x] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version of the `main` branch\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.tabline\n\n### Neovim version\n\n0.11.x\n\n### Description\n\nI presume this may not be considered a \"bug\" and @echasnovski feel free to close this out and/or convert to a discussion or whatever you see appropriate, but I wanted to have this here to help guide users to the solution to avoid you getting flooded with a bunch of GH issues / questions.\n\nGiven the newest breaking change here fe8a669 the tabline is not shown anymore if you are using Snacks dashboard. Snacks dashboard appears to set `showtabline` to `0` and since it loads before anything else, mini.tabline now will not show because it is no longer overriding vim options that are already set.\n\nThe solution for me was to add to my options config on startup `vim.o.showtabline = 2`. This is because I prefer to use the default setup config for plugins like mini.tabline (i.e., `require('mini.tabline').setup({})`) whenever possible so I don't have to micromanage custom options and breaking changes with plugins.\n\nHope this helps others and helps minimize the Issues / Questions that come to you @echasnovski ;-)\n\n### Reproduction\n\nN/A",
