        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "@echasnovski another thought since plugin configurations are all just a giant game of \"what does the plugin author think is the most sane default the user wants\" ... is to have the mini tabline default option set to change the showtabline to 2 but allows the user to change the config options to preserve the option if they desire (how the new breaking change functions). In other words, I think it is perfectly reasonable if the user is installing the mini.tabline plugin that their intent is to show the tabline. So that should be the default... but there is an option they can set to preserve the vim option if they want to for whatever reason.\n\nI just think it is more confusing / more trouble for a user who installs mini.tabline to have them have to explicitly set in their config they want showtablien=2 when more than likely their expectation is that mini.tabline does that for them when they choose to install the plugin.\n\nHopefully that makes sense...",
