        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> In other words, I think it is perfectly reasonable if the user is installing the mini.tabline plugin that their intent is to show the tabline. So that should be the default... but there is an option they can set to preserve the vim option if they want to for whatever reason.\n\nIt does start to look like this is indeed a reasonable behavior for 'mini.tabline' to force `showtabline=2` as it is basically essential to module's functionality. But there won't be going back to `set_vim_settings` type of configuration, as this is basically a config overengineering and I wanted to remove them for quite some time now.\n\nI have to have an overnight thinking about this one.",
