        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "> But there won't be going back to `set_vim_settings` type of configuration, as this is basically a config overengineering and I wanted to remove them for quite some time now.\n\nMakes total sense! I would say then it is perfectly reasonable to just put something in the docs that states mini.tabline is setting the showtabline=2 vim option and if the user needs it to operate differently they need to override it themselves however they see fit. But I can't really think of a valid reason someone would want to... so a simple note in the docs seems valid. A note in the docs probably isn't even required but to save yourself the trouble down the road it allows you to say \"read the docs please\" ;-)",
